### Problem description & steps to reproduce

Tool calls emitted by Ministral-3 during reasoning (inside the [THINK]...[/THINK] block) will not be processed by the parser. 

## Steps to reproduce: 

This issue occurs if you try to use this model for agentic workloads in Open WebUI and give it any access to tool-calling. First assistant turn usually works fine, second turn, the tool call gets piped into the reasoning.

To enable reasoning, the system prompt must contain Mistral's official prompt, which can be found here: https://huggingface.co/mistralai/Ministral-3-14B-Reasoning-2512/blob/main/SYSTEM_PROMPT.txt

After 4 h of work and several euros in API cost, trying to cleanly reproduce the issue, I've only been able to reproduce it exactly once outside Open WebUI. Request and response are in the logs below. However, in Open WebUI, I can reproduce it very reliably in any chat where web search or RAG is used. Feel free to delete this report if you believe it misplaced.

That said, the proposed change in the paragraph below completely fixes the issue for me, which I why I hope that this might still be a good patch for the Ministral-3 parser here in llama.cpp.

## Proposed fix: 

In `common/parsers/ministral3.cpp`, line 77-78, replace the following lines:
```
        auto reasoning =
            extract_reasoning ? p.optional("[THINK]" + p.reasoning(p.until("[/THINK]")) + "[/THINK]") : p.eps();
```

With the following:
```
        auto reasoning =
            extract_reasoning ? p.optional("[THINK]" + p.reasoning(p.until_one_of({"[/THINK]", "[TOOL_CALLS]"})) + p.optional(p.literal("[/THINK]"))) : p.eps();
```

This allows the model to emit tool calls during CoT reasoning, similar to how deepseek.cpp is handling it.

Disclaimer: Code is AI generated, and I'm a total C++ noob, so I am hesitant to make any commits or PRs here.

However, changing the line above, under my conditions, turned the model from being nearly unable to make any tool calls, to actually doing proper agentic loops with 10-20 tool calls in a single turn. 


